\begin{abstract}
This document provides an intentionally adversarial technical critique of L-ToEC v4.4.
The framework has clearly crossed into a higher tier of rigor; as a result, its remaining
weaknesses are now structural rather than conceptual. The critique targets (i) overconstraint
and circular necessity, (ii) semantic inflation of computational language, (iii) misuse of
universality theorems as explanatory closure, and (iv) the risk that falsifiability is more
performative than load-bearing. Each criticism is accompanied by an explicit failure mode
that a hostile referee would exploit.
\end{abstract}

